      "message": "A huge amount of churn in this CL is caused just by renaming \"error reporter\" to \"error handler\" in a ton of places.\n\nI am OK with the name \"error reporter\" and don\u0027t think it\u0027s worth any churn to change the name. It was a useful distinction when we had two things (an SkSL::ErrorReporter and a dsl::ErrorHandler) but now there is only one and I think the name change is not needed anymore.\n\nI mentioned in chat that I would rather not put all error handling under the \"DSL\" umbrella, as handling errors is something that all SkSL will need to do, not just DSL. I think my ideal would be:\n\n- Bring back SkSLErrorReporter.h\n",
      "revId": "890b9887727b148d655c053732c05d21a15db587",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
